-- Classic 1.60: Forever calibration of pet base health (pet_levelstats).
--
-- WHY: hunter pet and most warlock demon base health is based on a vanilla Classic Era
-- VMaNGOS import, with later local adjustments for Imp and Voidwalker. On official Forever, Blizzard
-- deliberately buffed pet base health above vanilla during the November 2026 hotfix passes, so pets
-- here are roughly 13% squishier than the official design intent at every level - at 60 a hunter pet
-- is missing ~458 health, a voidwalker ~565. Since owner-stat scaling (however implemented) builds
-- multiplicatively/additively on top of these base values, being wrong here makes every pet wrong
-- everywhere, geared or not. Separately, the Forever incubus demon has no rows in this table at all
-- and falls back to generated placeholder stats (flat 22/22/25/28 attributes) - outright broken
-- rather than merely miscalibrated. The evidence chain for each number applied here follows, and is
-- the further documentation for this change.
--
-- Our baseline is a VMaNGOS vanilla import with the subsequent Imp curve and Voidwalker +40
-- adjustments (2026_10_28_82 / 2026_11_09_61). Official Forever buffs
-- pet base health over vanilla. Sources (primary first):
--   * Blizzard, WoW: Forever Hotfixes - November 25, 2026 (rolling archive):
--     https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24315281/wow-forever-hotfixes-november-25-2026
--       Nov 6:  'Voidwalker base health increased by about 40 at all levels' (flat, not per-level)
--       Nov 10: 'Voidwalker base Health increased by ~15%' (on top of the Nov 6 +40)
--       Nov 10: 'Imp/Incubus/Succubus base Health increased by ~15%' + Imp Firebolt ranks 1-4 base dmg up
--       Nov 10: 'Fixed a bug where Pets erroneously had 150% of their normal health ... corrected to 115%'
--   * wowfdb.com/classes/hunter/pets/  - 'A pet has 115% of its normal health'
--   * wowfdb.com/classes/warlock/changes/ - Nov 11 entry confirming demon +15% (felhunter NOT included)
--   * warcrafttavern.com/forever/news/voidwalker-health-increased-wow-forever-hotfixes-for-november-6/
--     and wowforeverguides.com/news/wowforever-hotfixes-raise-voidwalker-health-and-lower-tanning-rack
--     - independent confirmations of the flat +40 voidwalker bump
-- Applied here: hunter pets (entry 1, covers every hunter pet) hp x1.15; Imp 416 / Succubus 1863
-- hp x1.15; Voidwalker 1860 (vanilla hp+40) x1.15 (the +40 inside the multiplier is the natural reading;
-- the alternative differs by only ~6hp at 60). Felhunter 417 deliberately unchanged, matching
-- official. Armor, mana and stats untouched - no source shows them changing.
-- Incubus: the Forever succubus-counterpart demon (PET_INCUBUS=184600, NPC_CWD_INCUBUS=185317 in
-- core) has NO pet_levelstats rows at all and falls back to generated placeholder stats. Official
-- includes incubus in the +15%; the core treats it as DemonKind::Succubus everywhere. Rows here
-- mirror the succubus curve x1.15 for both incubus entries. Neither has ever been summoned on this
-- server (character_pet is empty for them), so this is pure upside. If the actual summon entry turns
-- out to be a third one (184312/185335), it is no worse off than before.
-- Idempotent: fixed values. PR rationale: this is a DATA calibration, independent of the pet
-- gear-scaling aura implementation - either can be adopted without the other.
DELETE FROM `pet_levelstats` WHERE `creature_entry` IN (1,416,1860,1863) AND `level` <= 63;
DELETE FROM `pet_levelstats` WHERE `creature_entry` IN (184600,185317);
